<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alexander Stubb</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1968">1968</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alexander Stubb is a Finnish politician of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-coalition-party">National Coalition Party</a> who served as foreign minister, prime minister in 2014–2015 and finance minister. After several years in academic and European posts, he won the presidential election of 2024 and took office as president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a> on 1 March 2024, shortly after Finland had joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nato">NATO</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alexander-stubb.jpg" alt="Alexander Stubb" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The White House · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Finnish_President_Alexander_Stubb_arrives_to_the_South_Portico_of_the_White_House_for_a_meeting_with_President_Donald_Trump_(54732037329)_(cropped_2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
